From 251e4cb57912c0d2dd7b5f5e54cb2bc79f6a4d2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: praveenxsharma <itachisec@duck.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:49:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] minuitwrp: Default to a single layer mixer

MTK topology parsing knows only the A11-era topology names; on the
OOS13 (4.19) kernels the mode_properties blob does not match and the
fallback of 2 LMs splits the framebuffer across two half-width
planes. On single-LCM devices (karen: one panel, one DSI link) this
renders the UI through a half-width path - complete UI squeezed into
a narrow strip. Default to 1 LM; dual-LM devices parse their topology
explicitly anyway.

Verified on karen (OnePlus Nord 2T, OOS13 kernel): TWRP renders the
full 1080x2400 UI correctly with 1 LM.
---
 minuitwrp/graphics_drm.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/minuitwrp/graphics_drm.cpp b/minuitwrp/graphics_drm.cpp
index 99ebd28..5eb7bbf 100644
--- a/minuitwrp/graphics_drm.cpp
+++ b/minuitwrp/graphics_drm.cpp
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@ struct drm_surface {
 
 #define NUM_MAIN 1
 #define NUM_PLANES 4
-#define DEFAULT_NUM_LMS 2
+#define DEFAULT_NUM_LMS 1
 
 struct Crtc {
   drmModeObjectProperties *props;
-- 
2.43.0

